sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task, DECISIONS R1-R4, 5 (swamp role SSH identity), round 2 bugs (server admin password by its own vault key, cleanup on pass or fail). docs/reference/database-servers.md.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: database:create
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as Node 12<br/>beast-mysql server
  CLI->>GW: database:create shop<br/>--server=beast-mysql --instance=42
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit database:create shop --server=beast-mysql --instance=42`
  %%> - syntax: `<slug> --server=SERVER [--instance=ID] [--locale=C|C.UTF-8] [--test-processes=N]`
  %%> - or, to register an existing database: `<slug> --driver=DRIVER [--host=HOST] [--port=PORT] [--database=NAME] [--path=PATH] [--username=USER] [--password=SECRET] [--node=NODE]`
  %%> - on a Valkey server: `<slug> --server=SERVER --pattern=PATTERN ... --allow=RULE ... [--database=INDEX]`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - the connection slug as the argument: lowercase kebab, at most 63 characters
  %%> - with `--server`: the Database server that gets the new database
  %%> - with `--instance`: the Instance that owns the database and gets it attached under prefix `DB`
  %%> Who can call it:
  %%> - the `orbit` CLI and the MCP tool send the same request
  Note over GW: Validate, reserve the name<br/>connection: creating · task #5121
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the slug `shop` is free (`database.slug_conflict`)
  %%> - with `--server`: Database server `beast-mysql` is active, and your Node has an access grant to Node 12
  %%> - with `--instance`: Instance 42 exists, and the server is MySQL or PostgreSQL (`database.driver_unsupported` for Valkey)
  %%> - `--locale` and `--test-processes` only on PostgreSQL; `--pattern` and `--allow` only on Valkey
  %%> - no database removal runs on `beast-mysql`; the Gateway holds one lock per Database server
  %%> Builds:
  %%> - the names from the slug: database `shop`, test database `shop_test`, owner `<project>_<instance>`
  %%> - a new owner password, or the existing one when Instance 42 already has an owner on this server
  %%> Decides:
  %%> - whether this is a registration of an existing database, or a new database on a server
  alt registration, no --server
    Note over GW: Record the connection<br/>R1: no run · password encrypted
    %%> When:
    %%> - `--driver` registers a database that already exists, for example on another host or a SQLite file
    %%> Result:
    %%> - connection `shop` is recorded, with its password encrypted
    %%> - no task and no Swamp run start (R1); nothing changes on any Node
    GW-->>CLI: 201 Created<br/>connection shop
    %%> What you get:
    %%> - the connection record at once; there is nothing to follow
  else new database on a server
    GW->>SW: Store the owner password<br/>database-create-intent-5121
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - puts the owner password into the Swamp vault on Node 209, after the task is committed (R3)
    %%> Not included:
    %%> - the server's admin password; it is already in the vault under the server's own key `database-server-3-admin`
    %%> Why:
    %%> - secrets go Gateway → vault → step; workflow inputs carry only vault key names
    GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-database-create
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - starts one Swamp run on serve (Node 209)
    %%> Inputs:
    %%> - the driver, database names, owner name, test pool size and locale
    %%> - the vault key names `database-create-intent-5121` and `database-server-3-admin`
    %%> - Node 12's address and SSH host keys; the SSH identity comes from the `swamp` role
    GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5121
    %%> What you get:
    %%> - the task number, at once
    %%> Next:
    %%> - the CLI follows the task with `operation:show`
    SW->>N: Copy the action scripts<br/>@swamp/ssh copy · /tmp/…-5121
    %%> How:
    %%> - Swamp reaches Node 12 over SSH from 209 with the official `@swamp/ssh` behavior
    %%> - the SSH identity is the one the `swamp` role owns, at its one role-defined place
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - copies the shipped action scripts into `/tmp/orbit-database-create-5121`
    SW->>N: Check names are free<br/>probe owner and databases
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - checks that the database names and the owner are unused, or already belong to this connection
    %%> Refuses:
    %%> - a name the server already has for something else (`database.name_conflict`); nothing changes
    %%> How:
    %%> - each script runs the fixed `mysql`, `psql` or Valkey client inside the server container
    %%> - the step reads both passwords with `vault.get` and passes them on standard input, never in argv
    SW->>N: Create the owner<br/>login with the owner password
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - creates the owner login, or keeps it when it already exists with this password
    %%> Per driver:
    %%> - MySQL, PostgreSQL: one owner per Instance on a server; a second database for Instance 42 reuses it
    %%> - Valkey: `ACL SETUSER shop reset on #<hash> resetchannels ~<pattern> -@all +<rule> -@admin -@dangerous`
    SW->>N: Create the databases<br/>shop, shop_test, test pool
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - creates the primary database, and with `--instance` the test database
    %%> Per driver:
    %%> - PostgreSQL: also `shop_test_test_1` to `_8`, with the chosen locale and `TEMPLATE template0`
    %%> - Valkey: no database; the connection records index 1, checked against the live server
    SW->>N: Grant the owner access<br/>only its own databases
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - grants the owner its databases and test databases, nothing else
    %%> Per driver:
    %%> - MySQL: one grant per database, plus one for the test prefix
    %%> - PostgreSQL: revokes PUBLIC access, then grants the public schema to the owner
    %%> - Valkey: `ACL SAVE`, so the user survives a restart
    SW->>N: Check the owner login<br/>log in as the owner
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - logs in as the owner and checks it reaches each new database
    %%> Why:
    %%> - the connection only counts as active when the server accepts it
    SW->>N: Remove the scripts<br/>always runs · rm -rf /tmp/…-5121
    %%> When:
    %%> - always, after the steps above, whether they passed or failed
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - removes `/tmp/orbit-database-create-5121`, so no scripts stay on Node 12
    %%> If it fails:
    %%> - the task result does not change; the directory holds no secrets
    alt every step passes
      N-->>SW: owner logs in
      %%> Returns:
      %%> - the check passed for every database
      SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
      %%> How the Gateway learns it:
      %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway
      Note over GW: Activate the connection<br/>attach to Instance 42 · DB
      %%> Result:
      %%> - connection `shop` becomes active, linked to `beast-mysql`, with Node 12's address and port
      %%> - with `--instance`: Instance 42 owns it and gets its `DB_*` keys; run `env:sync` to install them
      %%> - task #5121 succeeds
    else a step fails
      N--xSW: name taken or exit ≠ 0
      %%> When:
      %%> - a name is taken, SQL fails, SSH fails, or the owner cannot log in
      SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
      %%> The Gateway reads:
      %%> - which step failed and its error code
      Note over GW: Mark the connection failed<br/>task failed · rerun after a fix
      %%> Result:
      %%> - connection `shop` stays reserved, marked failed, with its encrypted owner password
      %%> - task #5121 fails
      %%> On the Node:
      %%> - an owner or database created before the failure stays; there is no rollback
      %%> - that is safe: the name check accepts objects that already belong to this connection
      %%> Retry:
      %%> - run the same command again; it reuses the reservation and finishes the missing steps
      %%> - a changed request is a conflict (`database.slug_conflict`)
    end
    loop every 2 s until terminal
      CLI->>GW: operation:show #5121
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - asks for the task's status every 2 seconds until it has ended
      GW-->>CLI: status + result
      %%> Returns:
      %%> - the current status, and the result once the task has ended
    end
  end
